\pard\keepn\sb240\sa150\f0\fs29\b\cf1 Claims to avoid in discussion\b0\par
\pard\li720\fi-300\tx720\sa65\f0\fs21\cf1\bullet\tab Do not say that any named product is endorsed, preferred or proven superior.\par
\pard\li720\fi-300\tx720\sa65\f0\fs21\cf1\bullet\tab Do not promise that a scribe saves a particular amount of time, prevents burnout or improves patient outcomes.\par
\pard\li720\fi-300\tx720\sa65\f0\fs21\cf1\bullet\tab Do not describe a public general-purpose chatbot as appropriate patient-specific diagnostic or prescribing support.\par
\pard\li720\fi-300\tx720\sa65\f0\fs21\cf1\bullet\tab Do not imply that citations make a generated answer correct or complete.\par
\pard\li720\fi-300\tx720\sa65\f0\fs21\cf1\bullet\tab Do not imply that remote monitoring means continuous observation.\par
\pard\li720\fi-300\tx720\sa65\f0\fs21\cf1\bullet\tab Do not present machine translation as a replacement for professional interpreting in complex clinical communication or consent.\par
\pard\li720\fi-300\tx720\sa65\f0\fs21\cf1\bullet\tab Do not imply that treatment optimisation is available as a general Australian GP system.\par
\pard\li720\fi-300\tx720\sa65\f0\fs21\cf1\bullet\tab Do not use the glaucoma-screening performance figures as diabetic-retinopathy performance figures.\par
\pard\li720\fi-300\tx720\sa65\f0\fs21\cf1\bullet\tab Do not provide a numerical answer about prostate artery embolisation without separate clinical research and review.\par
